                {
                  "code": "INTRO_COORD_101",
                  "title": "Introduction to Coordinate Geometry",
                  "image": "intro_coord.jpg",
                  "duration": 800,
                  "content": "Coordinate geometry is the study of geometry using a coordinate system. It involves plotting points, lines, and curves on a plane using coordinates (x, y). It is used to solve problems related to distances, midpoints, slopes, and equations of lines."
                },
                {
                  "code": "DISTANCE_COORD_102",
                  "title": "Distance and Midpoint Formulas",
                  "image": "distance_midpoint.jpg",
                  "duration": 800,
                  "content": "The distance between two points (x₁, y₁) and (x₂, y₂) is given by √((x₂ - x₁)² + (y₂ - y₁)²). The midpoint of a line segment joining two points (x₁, y₁) and (x₂, y₂) is ((x₁ + x₂)/2, (y₁ + y₂)/2)."
                },
                {
                  "code": "SLOPE_COORD_103",
                  "title": "Slope and Equation of a Line",
                  "image": "slope_line.jpg",
                  "duration": 800,
                  "content": "The slope of a line passing through two points (x₁, y₁) and (x₂, y₂) is (y₂ - y₁)/(x₂ - x₁). The equation of a line in slope-intercept form is y = mx + b, where m is the slope and b is the y-intercept."
                }
              ],
              "videos": [],
              "audios": [],
              "tests": [
