                  "title": "Vocabulary Development",
                  "image": "vocab_development.jpg",
                  "duration": 1200,
                  "content": "Vocabulary development refers to the process of learning and expanding the set of words a person can understand and use in communication. It involves recognizing new words, understanding their meanings, and using them correctly in context. This process enhances both spoken and written communication skills, boosts reading comprehension, and enriches overall language use. Effective methods of vocabulary development include reading widely, using word maps, playing word games, and practicing contextual word usage."
                },
                {
                  "code": "WORD_FORM_102",
                  "title": "Word Formation",
                  "image": "word_formation.jpg",
                  "duration": 1200,
                  "content": "Word formation is the process of creating new words in a language. This can be achieved through various methods such as: 1. Affixation: Adding prefixes or suffixes to base words, e.g., 'unhappy', 'kindness'. 2. Compounding: Joining two or more words to create a new word, e.g., 'toothbrush', 'notebook'. 3. Conversion: Changing a word's class without altering its form, e.g., 'to email', 'to Google'. 4. Blending: Combining parts of two words, e.g., 'brunch' (breakfast + lunch). 5. Clipping: Shortening longer words, e.g., 'info' (information), 'ad' (advertisement). Understanding these processes helps improve language creativity and fluency."
                }
              ],
