                    "instruction": "Let equal sides be x, hypotenuse = x√2. Perimeter = 2x + x√2 = x(2+√2) = 2. Solve for x, then longer side = x√2.",
                    "code": "JMATH_23_008"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "Tickets for the school play were priced at ₦520.00 each for adults and ₦250.00 each for kids. How many kids' tickets were sold if the total sales were ₦171,000.00 and there were 5 times as many adult tickets sold as children's tickets?",
                    "correctAnswer": "60",
                    "options": ["50", "55", "60", "65"],
                    "instruction": "Let x = kids' tickets. Adults = 5x. Total sales = 520(5x) + 250x = 2600x + 250x = 2850x = 171000 → x = 60 [citation:1].",
                    "code": "JMATH_23_009"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "A ship sets sail from port A (86°N, 56°W) for port B (86°N, 64°W), which is close by. Find the distance the ship covered from port A to port B, correct to the nearest km. (Take π = 3.142 and R = 6370 km).",
                    "correctAnswer": "556 km",
                    "options": ["445 km", "556 km", "668 km", "779 km"],
                    "instruction": "Distance along latitude = (difference in longitude in radians) × R × cos(latitude). Δλ = 8° = 8 × π/180 rad. Distance = 6370 × (8π/180) × cos 86°.",
                    "code": "JMATH_23_010"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "A rectangular plot of land has sides with lengths of 38 m and 52 m correct to the nearest m. Find the range of the possible values of the area of the rectangle.",
