                  {
                    "question": "A man sells different brands of items. 1/9 of the items are from Brand A, 5/8 of the remainder are from Brand B and the rest are from Brand C. If the total number of Brand C items is 81, how many more Brand B items than Brand C does the shop have?",
                    "correctAnswer": "54",
                    "options": ["27", "54", "81", "108"],
                    "instruction": "Let total = T. A = T/9, remainder = 8T/9. B = (5/8)×(8T/9) = 5T/9. C = T - (T/9 + 5T/9) = T - 6T/9 = 3T/9 = T/3 = 81 → T = 243. B = 5×243/9 = 135. B - C = 135 - 81 = 54 [citation:1].",
                    "code": "JMATH_23_016"
